[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Feather Mail has been installed to %%PREFIX%%/feather.

1. CONFIGURE
   Sample configs were installed as:
     %%ETCDIR%%/server.exs.sample
     %%ETCDIR%%/pipeline.exs.sample

   Copy and edit them:
     cp %%ETCDIR%%/server.exs.sample %%ETCDIR%%/server.exs
     cp %%ETCDIR%%/pipeline.exs.sample %%ETCDIR%%/pipeline.exs
     edit %%ETCDIR%%/server.exs %%ETCDIR%%/pipeline.exs

   Override the config directory with the FEATHER_CONFIG_FOLDER env var.

2. PRIVILEGED PORTS
   Feather binds SMTP ports 25/465/587. By default the service runs as the
   unprivileged "feather" user, which CANNOT bind ports below 1024 without
   extra configuration. Either:
     - run as root:  sysrc feather_user="root"
     - or grant the feather user low-port access via mac_portacl(4).

3. ENABLE AND START
     sysrc feather_enable="YES"
     service feather start

   Logs:  %%FEATHER_LOGDIR%%/
   Docs:  https://github.com/yoonka/feather
EOM
}
]
